  "notes": [
    "**Gustar** is a regular **-AR verb**",
    "No spelling changes or stem changes",
    "**SPECIAL USAGE:** Gustar works differently than English \"to like\"",
    "Structure: **Indirect object pronoun + gusta/gustan + subject**",
    "*Me gusta el café* = I like coffee (literally: Coffee pleases me)",
    "*Me gustan los libros* = I like books (literally: Books please me)",
    "Most commonly used in 3rd person: **gusta** (singular) / **gustan** (plural)",
    "Indirect object pronouns: me, te, le, nos, les",
    "Common usage:",
    "*Me gusta bailar* (I like to dance)",
    "*¿Te gusta el chocolate?* (Do you like chocolate?)",
    "*A ella le gustan las películas* (She likes movies)",
    "Similar verbs: **encantar** (to love), **interesar** (to interest), **molestar** (to bother)#v"
  ],
